          <div>
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-slate-900 mb-3">1. The Fatal Danger of Cow's Milk: Why KMR is Mandatory</h2>
            <p>
              Every week at Rehman Veterinary Clinic in Lahore, we witness heartbreaking cases where well-meaning rescuers feed newborn kittens cow's milk, buffalo milk, or packaged supermarket milk (such as Olper's or MilkPak). Within 24 to 48 hours, these kittens develop explosive watery diarrhea, hypothermia, severe abdominal bloating, and rapid dehydration leading to death.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-3">
              Feline maternal milk contains <strong>almost double the protein</strong> and <strong>more than triple the fat</strong> of cow's milk, but less than half the lactose (milk sugar). Kittens lack the lactase enzyme necessary to break down bovine lactose. The undigested lactose draws water into the colon, causing fatal osmotic diarrhea.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-3 font-semibold text-emerald-900">
              The only clinically verified replacement for mother cat milk is <strong>KMR (Kitten Milk Replacer)</strong>. It is chemically balanced with 40% crude protein, 28% crude fat, and essential taurine, replicating the exact maternal nutritional profile.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-slate-900 mb-3">2. How to Mix &amp; Prepare KMR Powder Correctly</h2>
            <p>
              Improper mixing causes either nutrient starvation (if too diluted) or severe constipation and fecal impaction (if too concentrated). Follow this precise clinical ratio:
            </p>
            <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-white border border-slate-200 shadow-sm mt-3 space-y-3">
              <div class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-900">Standard Dilution Ratio:</div>
              <div class="inline-block px-4 py-2 bg-emerald-50 text-emerald-800 font-black rounded-xl text-xs">
                1 Part KMR Powder : 2 Parts Warm Boiled Water
              </div>
              <ul class="text-xs text-slate-600 space-y-2 list-disc list-inside mt-2">
                <li><strong>Temperature Control:</strong> Boil clean filtered water and let it cool to approximately 100°F (38°C) before mixing. Never use boiling water, which destroys active enzymes and vitamins.</li>
                <li><strong>Smooth Blending:</strong> Stir or whisk vigorously to eliminate all clumps. Powder lumps can block nursing bottle teats.</li>
                <li><strong>Storage Shelf Life:</strong> Mixed liquid KMR must be refrigerated immediately and used within 24 hours. Never microwave kitten milk—it creates hot spots that severely scald the kitten's tongue and esophagus. Warm the bottle in a bowl of hot water instead.</li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </div>

